# Cloudflare static-assets headers.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Security headers, site-wide.
#
# The audit found none were being sent. This is a static site with no cookies,
# no login and no user input, so the exposure is limited — but these are free
# and Google treats HTTPS/security hygiene as a quality signal.
#
# CSP is deliberately strict because the site genuinely needs nothing exotic:
# no third-party scripts, no inline event handlers, no external stylesheets.
# 'unsafe-inline' is required for style-src only because Next injects inline
# styles; script-src stays clean. Revisit if analytics are added in Phase 7 —
# a GA4 tag will need its domain allow-listed here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRE-LAUNCH ONLY — REMOVE BEFORE GOING LIVE ON THE REAL DOMAIN.
#
# The site is currently served from a public *.workers.dev preview URL while
# urgencemedicale.ma is not yet registered. robots.txt says Allow: / and every
# canonical points at the unregistered domain, so without this Google could
# index the preview host and split signals against the real site later.
#
# Deleting this block is item 1 on PRE-LAUNCH-CHECKLIST.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Next's metadata routes emit real PNGs at extensionless paths (/icon,
# /opengraph-image). Without an extension the asset server falls back to
# application/octet-stream, and WhatsApp/Facebook then refuse to render the
# share preview — which matters here because WhatsApp is a primary channel
# for this market. These rules pin the correct type.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/icon
  Content-Type: image/png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# Content-hashed build output is immutable by construction.
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
